window.products.push({"id":645959,"name":"Aermate AMT001 Aerate Wine While Still in The Bottle, Stainless Steel","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71JcK8GADcL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"No mess, in-bottle aeration system. Aermate is the only aerator that can perform in-glass aeration on red wine, white wine, and spirits. Why aerate at all? Wine Aeration reduces tannins (chemical compounds that create aftertaste), acidity and sulfites (which some people can be allergic to). The aeration of wine and spirits improves taste, smoothens aftertaste, awakens the natural aroma of the product, and enhances the drinkability of your favorite beverage. What is the Aermate Aerator? The Aermate Aerator is an effective in-bottle or in-glass aerator that aerates all wines and spirits. The Aerator is constructed of food grade stainless steel and silicone. Our aerator is rugged, repeatable and simple to use – just squeeze the bulb. Our patent pending design includes a Microbubble Tip at the end of the aerator that breaks air from the bulb into tiny bubbles that diffuse easily into the wine or spirit, providing instant, effective aeration. The Aermate Aerator is simple to clean – just rinse the stem and Microbubble Tip with hot water and dry by squeezing the bulb, and to store, just place it in a drawer, there is no special stand or holder required. Our rugged, repeatable, instantaneous and effective aerator is a perfect gift for the aficionado, the casual drinker and anyone in between. Why is the Aermate Aerator better than other aerators? Decanters take time, break easily and are difficult to clean. Single pour aeration systems are messy, splatter and give the user only one shot at aeration. The Aermate Aerator performs in-glass or in-bottle aeration, which means that our aerator does not need to be present during the pour. Aeration can be performed in the bottle before the pour, for example in another room, or after the pour, for example in a restaurant or on an airplane. Pouring systems simply do not provide such flexibility. The Aermate Aerator allows you to aerate more or less as needed or desired: use one squeeze for a glass of petite sirah, use three squeezes for a glass of bold cabernet, etc. The Aermate Aerator allows you to squeeze until you are satisfied. Again, pouring systems do not provide this flexibility. The Aermate Aerator is also extremely simple to use, just place the Microbubble Tip at the bottom of the bottle or glass and start squeezing. Pouring systems on the other hand, require alignment between the bottle, aerator and glass. Which drinks can benefit from the Aermate Aerator? Wine is not the only beverage benefiting from proper aeration. Spirits aged in casks likewise open and reach their full flavor potential when aerated. With the Aermate Aerator there is no need to change aerators depending upon what you are imbibing. One tool enables you to bring out the hidden aromas and flavors of any wine or spirit instantly! Our aerator is great for aerating: red wine, white wine, bourbon, brandy, cognac, gin, liqueur, gum, scotch, tequila whiskey, and more. The Aermate Aerator works using three natural principles: Diffusion: The Aermate Aerator uses its Microbubble Tip to deliver air in the form of tiny microbubbles that break down and increase surface area contact between the liquid and air. Increased contact area maximizes oxygen exposure and total air volume delivered. Diffusion: The Aermate Aerator uses its Microbubble Tip to deliver air in the form of tiny microbubbles that break down and increase surface area contact between the liquid and air. Increased contact area maximizes oxygen exposure and total air volume delivered. Buoyancy: The Aermate Aerator delivers air to the base of the bottle or glass, allowing the exposed oxygen to flow up through the entire beverage. Buoyancy: The Aermate Aerator delivers air to the base of the bottle or glass, allowing the exposed oxygen to flow up through the entire beverage. Mixing: The Aermate Aerator gently stirs through the liquid while diffusing air. The stirring further enhances oxygen exposure to all areas of the beverage. Mixing: The Aermate Aerator gently stirs through the liquid while diffusing air. The stirring further enhances oxygen exposure to all areas of the beverage. Why choose the Aermate Aerator? The Aermate Wine & Spirits Aerator provides an innovative, effective and fun way to aerate a variety of beverages. Our aerator is utilitarian and provides long term durability: there is no plastic to break or crack, and it stores in your kitchen drawer for easy access. The aerator is sleek, rugged, simple to use and clean, and allows you to aerate to your individual taste, unlike the messy pouring systems that are slow, splatter and spill. The Aermate Aerator can aerate an entire bottle or a single glass in seconds as opposed to hours in a decanter, and aerates red and white wines, liquors and spirits. AERMATE and MICROBUBBLE are federally registered trademarks of Aermate Products LLC. The Aermate Wine and Spirits Aerator is more versatile than any other aerator on the market. Let’s see how it compares to the competition.AermateSoireeVint","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71JcK8GADcL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Aermate","source_asin":"B07FSC6QJJ","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-645959","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07FSC6QJJ","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B07FSC6QJJ","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
